/*! \mainpage gr-nut

A single, reusable interface between ffmpeg and GNU Radio for analogue
transmission chains: ffmpeg is the codec/format/sync layer, GNU Radio is
the physical layer, and a NUT stream over a pipe/FIFO is the socket
between them.

The module contains two blocks, one per direction. gr::nut::nut_source
ingests a strict-profile NUT stream (pcm_f32le audio + rawvideo/rgb24
video) and emits deinterleaved float audio (one port per channel) and
rgb24 video byte streams (one port per stream); the audio sample rate
and per-stream video geometry are adopted from the NUT stream headers at
start, the structure (stream kinds, codecs, channel count) is validated
and any mismatch is a hard error. gr::nut::nut_sink is the reverse: it
consumes float audio and rgb24 byte streams, muxes them into the same
profile with timestamps synthesized from sample/frame counts (the format
is declared via parameters — the sink writes the headers), and feeds
ffmpeg for encoding, recording, or streaming. In every chain there is at
most one clock — ffmpeg is paced purely by pipe backpressure.

See the repository README.md for the interface contract, clocking model
and error model, and docs/buffering.md for the buffering and
synchronization reference.

*/
